  "eyebrow": "Learning Path",
  "introHtml": "<p>A pragmatic learning path for those who already know the basics of C++ but have never had to run multiple threads within the same process without shooting themselves in the foot. We start with the bare minimum theory — what a thread really is and what can go wrong — and then move on to more sophisticated concepts. Each module ends with a project where you will put into practice what you have just learned.</p><p>The lessons should be completed in order: each project builds upon the concepts introduced in the theory immediately preceding it.</p><p>You can find all the source code for the course in this <a href=\"https://github.com/kineticCode-dev/MultithreadingLearningPath\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">repository</a>.</p>",
